# Overlay signing hashes file bytes exactly (Ed25519 over a sha256 of the
# folder). A Windows CI checkout with core.autocrlf would rewrite LF to CRLF in
# the working tree that electron-builder packs, changing those bytes and voiding
# every signature (the exact bug that shipped black overlays through beta.36).
#
# Pin all signed overlay text to LF on every platform so the packed bytes always
# equal the signed bytes. If you ever add a BINARY asset inside an overlay
# folder (png, jpg, font, ...), mark it `binary` here so it is never converted.
overlays/**/*.html  text eol=lf
overlays/**/*.css   text eol=lf
overlays/**/*.js    text eol=lf
overlays/**/*.json  text eol=lf
overlays/**/*.svg   text eol=lf
overlays/keys/*.pem text eol=lf

# Common binaries a designer might drop into an overlay folder: never convert.
overlays/**/*.png   binary
overlays/**/*.jpg   binary
overlays/**/*.jpeg  binary
overlays/**/*.gif   binary
overlays/**/*.webp  binary
overlays/**/*.ico   binary
overlays/**/*.woff  binary
overlays/**/*.woff2 binary
overlays/**/*.ttf   binary
